### ==========================================================
### ACCOUNTS — CRUD, cuenta default, archivar/restaurar (idempotentes)
### Las respuestas incluyen currency (estampada del usuario),
### openingBalance y createdAt/updatedAt.
### ==========================================================
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@email = tester@test.com
@password = SecureP@ss123

# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

###

@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Crear cuenta A (éxito) — la primera queda isDefault=true;
### currency la estampa el servidor (la del usuario)
# @name createA
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ahorros {{$randomInt 100 999}}", "type": "SAVINGS", "balance": 1000.50, "color": "TEAL" }

###

@accountA = {{createA.response.body.id}}

### Crear cuenta B (éxito)
# @name createB
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Efectivo {{$randomInt 100 999}}", "type": "CASH", "balance": 200, "color": "AMBER" }

###

@accountB = {{createB.response.body.id}}

### Listar cuentas (éxito)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get por id (éxito)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update nombre/color (éxito)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ahorros 2 {{$randomInt 100 999}}", "color": "BLUE" }

### Marcar B como default (éxito) — desmarca la anterior default
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountB}}/default
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Archivar A (soft delete) — solo funciona porque A ya NO es default
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Archivar A de nuevo — IDEMPOTENTE (200, no 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get de la archivada por id — SÍ responde (archivedAt la distingue)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Listar (A ya no aparece)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Listar incluyendo archivadas (A aparece con archivedAt != null)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts?includeArchived=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Restaurar con OTRO nombre — la salida cuando restore da 409 porque
### otra cuenta activa tomó el nombre mientras esta estaba archivada.
### Renombra y desarchiva en la misma escritura (atómico).
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}/restore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ahorros recuperada {{$randomInt 100 999}}" }

### Restaurar A — vuelve SIN isDefault (B conserva el default)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}/restore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Restaurar A de nuevo — IDEMPOTENTE (200 con el estado actual)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}/restore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- Casos de error ----------

### Archivar la cuenta DEFAULT (400 DEFAULT_ACCOUNT_ARCHIVE_BLOCKED)
### B es la default ahora — hay que marcar otra default primero.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountB}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update de una cuenta ARCHIVADA (400 RESOURCE_ARCHIVED) — archívala antes
# PUT {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "name": "no se puede" }

### Crear — tipo inválido (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "X", "type": "NOPE" }

### Crear — balance con 3 decimales (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "X", "type": "CASH", "balance": 10.555 }

### Mass assignment — balance/userId/currency directos (se ignoran)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Hack", "balance": 999999, "userId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "currency": "USD" }

### Get inexistente o de otro usuario (404 uniforme)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ==========================================================
### O-B1 — id del cliente (offline). El id lo pone el cliente y el
### servidor no lo reemplaza. Este bloque es re-ejecutable: la
### segunda corrida responde 200 (replay) en vez de 201.
### ==========================================================

### Crear con id propio (201 la primera vez, 200 el replay)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "019a0000-0b01-7000-8000-0000000000a1", "name": "Offline CASH", "type": "CASH", "balance": 100, "color": "TEAL" }

### Replay idéntico (200, mismo recurso, sin escribir de nuevo)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "019a0000-0b01-7000-8000-0000000000a1", "name": "Offline CASH", "type": "CASH", "balance": 100, "color": "TEAL" }

### Mismo id, payload distinto (409 ID_TAKEN)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "019a0000-0b01-7000-8000-0000000000a1", "name": "Otro nombre", "type": "CASH", "balance": 100 }

### id que no es UUID (400 VALIDATION)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "no-es-uuid", "name": "X", "type": "CASH" }

### id de OTRO usuario (409 ID_TAKEN opaco, no lee el documento ajeno).
### Para dispararlo: crea la cuenta con ese id logueado como otro usuario
### y repite este POST con el token de este.

### ==========================================================
### O-B2 — If-Match (concurrencia optimista). Sin la cabecera,
### la escritura es incondicional, como siempre.
### ==========================================================

### Leer la cuenta para quedarse con su updatedAt
# @name accForIfMatch
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

@accountAVersion = {{accForIfMatch.response.body.updatedAt}}

### Escritura con la versión correcta (200) — ojo: esto cambia updatedAt,
### así que repetirla tal cual da 409 STALE_UPDATE
PUT {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: {{accountAVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "color": "INDIGO" }

### La misma versión otra vez (409 STALE_UPDATE; `current` trae la cuenta del servidor)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: {{accountAVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "color": "ROSE" }

### Cabecera mal formada — fecha sin hora (400 VALIDATION, no un 409 silencioso)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: 2026-09-03
Content-Type: application/json

{ "color": "ROSE" }

### Archivar con versión vieja (409 STALE_UPDATE)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: 2020-01-01T00:00:00.000Z

### Cuenta default con versión vieja (409 STALE_UPDATE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountA}}/default
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: 2020-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
